From 3c62628e5a438599502fd09a86de1bd73d0b52e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:05:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] httpd: cross-site gate on every download row, safer handlers,
 Auto refresh kept (102.8 line)

- The cross-site gate covers every signed-in row with an output function of its own, not only
  names ending in .cgi; two unused rows that renewed the IKEv2 certificate on a GET are removed.
- Self-block guards use the client's MAC; the login state needs no shell; the iperf3 client
  request checks its port and lengths; the rules-engine switch and timer are committed when they
  change.
- The Traffic handler stamps the viewer file the traffic daemon reads; the Devices list uses the
  neighbour reader.
- Firewall > Status and Rule Status: Auto refresh is a router setting (two new defaults, off), so
  it survives a reboot, a flash and another browser; a click on its label works the switch.
- On the 102.8 line web.c also takes the 3006.102.10 hardening it lacked: a format string for
  every JSON and buffer write, the certificate file-name check before it is stored, the iperf3
  service whitelist, and bounds plus 64-bit start times in four diagnostic handlers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
